WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.200
Since 2016, when I got saved,

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.740
I've been studying the Bible.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.640
And it was all scattered.

4
00:00:10.315 --> 00:00:11.275
So I made one.

5
00:00:11.315 --> 00:00:14.795
Harvous is the app I've been wanting.

6
00:00:15.275 --> 00:00:16.435
Every day starts here.

7
00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.895
There's a passage waiting, and whatever I was

8
00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:21.095
in the middle of, so I can pick right back up.

9
00:00:21.135 --> 00:00:23.395
On my laptop, or on my phone.

10
00:00:28.108 --> 00:00:30.308
When I write, Harvous knows Scripture.

11
00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:32.208
I type a reference, and it becomes

12
00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:34.088
the verse, right there in my note.

13
00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:45.123
Tap a reference, and the passage opens right

14
00:00:45.163 --> 00:00:48.243
on the page, and stays put as I scroll.

15
00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:51.503
Cross-references are a tap away.

16
00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:54.043
So is every note I've written on it.

17
00:00:54.103 --> 00:00:56.283
And if a word catches me, the

18
00:00:56.323 --> 00:00:57.523
dictionary's right there.

19
00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.210
And when I open the Bible, those

20
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.150
same notes sit in the margin,

21
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.890
beside the verses they're about.

22
00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.869
Over time, it becomes my own study Bible.

23
00:01:18.693 --> 00:01:20.152
I never have to file anything.

24
00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:23.273
Harvous tags my notes, and sorts

25
00:01:23.313 --> 00:01:25.292
them into folders, on its own.

26
00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.163
And threads are mine.

27
00:01:32.683 --> 00:01:35.242
I pull one theme together, across

28
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:37.483
weeks of study, like everything I've

29
00:01:37.523 --> 00:01:39.143
been learning about the Holy Spirit.

30
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:41.823
I can share the whole thread with a link.

31
00:01:44.695 --> 00:01:46.935
And each note links to the others, so

32
00:01:46.975 --> 00:01:48.695
I can walk the whole line of thinking.

33
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:54.482
And the part I care about most.

34
00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:55.702
Harvous brings my study

35
00:01:55.742 --> 00:01:57.383
back, so it actually sticks.

36
00:01:57.423 --> 00:01:59.102
Not just what I read, but

37
00:01:59.143 --> 00:02:00.383
what I wrote about it.

38
00:02:02.268 --> 00:02:06.288
It's named after Proverbs 25:2.

39
00:02:06.548 --> 00:02:08.268
Studying the Bible is searching.

40
00:02:08.308 --> 00:02:10.527
Harvous is the place where the search

41
00:02:10.648 --> 00:02:13.488
settles into something you can come back to.

42
00:02:13.988 --> 00:02:15.608
I build it on my own, a little every week.

43
00:02:15.648 --> 00:02:17.188
If that sounds like what you've been

44
00:02:17.228 --> 00:02:19.328
looking for, I'd love for you to try it.

45
00:02:19.508 --> 00:02:20.828
And if it isn't there yet,

46
00:02:21.128 --> 00:02:22.968
write me, and tell me why.

